es":[],"unFigure":{"value":3663798,"what":"UN figure for 2025","date":"2025","forecast":true},"gapPct":1.6,"verdict":"matches","links":[{"label":"UN Statistics Division: births and deaths (table 3)","href":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/products/vitstats/seratab3.pdf"}]},{"key":"deaths","kind":"unsd","asOf":"2026-10-05","figure":{"value":3094593,"what":"deaths registered (registration reported as virtually complete)","date":"2025","provisional":false,"estimated":false},"notes":[],"unFigure":{"value":3089996,"what":"UN figure for 2025","date":"2025","forecast":true},"gapPct":-0.1,"verdict":"matches","links":[{"label":"UN Statistics Division: births and deaths (table 3)","href":"https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/products/vitstats/seratab3.pdf"}]},{"key":"net","kind":"researched","text":"Newer US numbers are much lower than the UN's 2024 forecast (1.18 million for 2026): the Census Bureau counted 1.26 million for July 2024–June 2025 and expects about 321,000 for the year to July 2026; the Congressional Budget Office projects 570,000 for 2026.","figure":{"value":321000,"what":"Census Bureau projection of net international migration, year to July 2026","date":"2026-07-01"},"unFigure":{"value":1177848,"what":"UN net migration forecast for 2026","date":"2026"},"gapPct":266.9,"verdict":"un-higher","links":[{"label":"Census Bureau, Jan 2026","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"},{"label":"CBO, Jan 2026","href":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61879"}],"quotes":[{"text":"Between July 1, 2024, and June 30, 2025, net international migration was 1.3 million, a notable drop from 2.7 million the year before (a decline of 53.8%). If current trends continue, net international migration is projected to be approximately 321,000 by July 2026, representing another decline of nearly 1 million since July 1, 2025.","href":"https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html"},{"text":"CBO now projects net immigration of 410,000 people (instead of 2.0 million) in 2025, 570,000 (instead of 1.6 million) in 2026, a total of 2.9 million (instead of 3.2 million) from 2028 to 2030, and 1.2 million (instead of 1.1 million) in 2035.","href":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61879"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"},{"key":"immigrants","kind":"researched","text":"Checks out: the Census Bureau's 2024 count is 50.2 million, plus 2.0 million born in Puerto Rico and the US island areas, whom the UN counts as born abroad. Both include people without legal status.","figure":{"value":52274689,"what":"Census Bureau 2024 foreign-born (50,234,858) plus people born in Puerto Rico (1,852,356) and the US island areas (187,475)","date":"2024"},"unFigure":{"value":52375047,"what":"UN DESA estimate for mid-2024","date":"2024-07-01"},"gapPct":0.2,"verdict":"matches","links":[{"label":"Census Bureau: the foreign-born","href":"https://www.census.gov/topics/population/foreign-born/about.html"},{"label":"Census Bureau ACS 2024, table B05002","href":"https://api.census.gov/data/2024/acs/acs1/groups/B05002.json"}],"quotes":[{"text":"anyone who is not a U.S. citizen at birth. This includes naturalized U.S. citizens, lawful permanent residents (immigrants), temporary migrants (such as foreign students), humanitarian migrants (such as refugees and asylees), and unauthorized migrants.","href":"https://www.census.gov/topics/population/foreign-born/about.html"}],"accessed":"2026-10-29"}],"links":{"self":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries/USA.json","countries":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/countries.json","risk":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/v1/risk.json","docs":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/api/","site":"https://fertility-tracker-live.vercel.app/country/USA"}}
